203:The complete learner state is saved at every checkpoint: connection strengths, eligibility traces and any slow 
stores the learner keeps (stage 1's learner has a reservoir state), the diary, the reservoir counter and every 
random-stream state. One lesson's update, receipt and diary admission are published together in one atomic write 
(temporary file, flush, rename), with SHA-256 hashes in the checkpoint manifest, so a resume never has one without the 
others. The replay that follows is published in its own atomic write (its update, its log entry and the random-stream 
states) before the next lesson starts, so a resume restarts at a lesson boundary. Resume goes into a new directory 
after checking input hashes. Test and validation processes receive only the learner state, never the diary.
